m1	78,282,1724,976		Gaelic air, probably an old bagpipe tune, in the treble clef with one sharp and 2/4 time, on three staves with the words "Blythe, blythe and merry are we" underlaid and D.C.; the third scale of five tones, without Third and Sixth.
m2	78,1205,1726,1488		Chinese temple hymn after Bitschurin, in the treble clef with one flat, on two staves of minims; an example of the fourth scale of five tones, without Fourth or Seventh.
m3	78,1870,1724,2817		Scotch air with tonic f sharp, in the treble clef with two sharps and 2/4 time, on four staves with the words "Will ye go, lassie, go To the braes o' Balquhidder" underlaid, marked Fine; the Second is absent and c sharp touched once.
